# MISTY MASI — PANINI CYCER SPECIFICATION
# Version: 1.0.0
# Status: Cycler construction from the retrieved/supplied MASI description
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# Misty MASI is the research / IPR / publication / provenance cycler for the
# Humanesque architecture.
#
# It is NOT merely a DOI generator.
# It governs the transition from research material and human contribution
# toward verifiable, attributable, temporally registered, reviewable and
# publishable records.
#
# The cycler is designed to operate across Humanesque cyclers and Epistemic
# Realms while preserving provenance, identity, temporal ordering, evidence,
# review state and publication state.
#
# PRIMARY DOI PATHS
# -----------------
# MISTY DOI:
#   Scholarly/publication path.
#   The workflow can obtain a conventional Zenodo DOI as part of the
#   publication/research workflow.
#
# TOK DOI:
#   Lightweight web-native temporal-registration path.
#   No token is intrinsically required.
#   The web record receives an OTS timestamp.
#   The record may be entered into a public registry if desired.
#   Registry material can subsequently be turned into a DOI according to
#   registry frequency / occupancy policy.
#
# GOVERNING INVARIANT
# -------------------
# MASI SHALL preserve and mark the provenance of human-originated inputs
# across Humanesque cyclers and their transformations, sufficient to support
# temporal-realm IPR attribution and evidentiary reconstruction within the
# Epistemic Realms.
#
# The provenance chain MUST NOT terminate at:
#   human -> cycler -> artifact
#
# It MUST remain traceable through relevant:
#   composition
#   transformation
#   branching
#   merging
#   editing
#   revision
#   versioning
#   publication
#   registration
#   downstream reuse
#
# ARCHITECTURAL POSITION
# ----------------------
# Human / Society
#       |
#       v
#   Epistemic Realm
#       |
#       +--> Research Kundali
#       |
#       v
#   Humanesque Cyclers
#       |
#       v
#   MEZ / Cycler Substrate
#       |
#       v
#   MISTY MASI
#       |
#       +--> Research / Publication
#       +--> Peer Review
#       +--> Journal
#       +--> Conference
#       +--> IPR / G3
#       +--> Provenance
#       +--> Temporal Registration
#       +--> Repository / DOI
#
# The production cyclers remain independent. Interoperability is provided
# through the shared cycler substrate / MEZ rather than by collapsing all
# cyclers into one workflow.
#
# RELATIONSHIPS
# ------------
# MASI
#   Research / IPR / publication process and governance cycler.
#
# MISTY
#   Publication / identity / provenance infrastructure associated with MASI.
#
# G3
#   Specific IPR / pre-filing gate within the MASI / IPR process.
#
# RESEARCH_KUNDALI
#   Research trajectory, provenance, review, lineage and epistemic-governance
#   structure used to keep Epistemic Realms clean.
#
# CYCLERS
#   Independent Humanesque production cyclers whose inputs and outputs can
#   enter MASI-governed research / IPR / publication workflows.
#
# MEZ
#   Shared interoperability / orchestration substrate. It does not erase
#   domain-specific cycler identity.
#
# DOMAIN SCOPE
# ------------
# MASI is domain-general at the governance/process level.
# It supports research artifacts and IPR/publication processes without
# requiring the domain to be enumerated as a fixed list of professions.
#
# FIRST-CLASS OBJECTS
# -------------------
# HUMAN_INPUT
# RESEARCH_OBJECT
# EVIDENCE_RECORD
# PROVENANCE_RECORD
# EPISTEMIC_RECORD
# RESEARCH_KUNDALI
# REVIEW_RECORD
# JOURNAL_RECORD
# CONFERENCE_RECORD
# IPR_RECORD
# G3_GATE
# REPOSITORY_RECORD
# MISTY_DOI_RECORD
# TOK_RECORD
# OTS_TIMESTAMP
# PUBLIC_REGISTRY_RECORD
# VERSION
# PUBLICATION_PACKAGE
# AUDIT_RECORD
# CLEARANCE_RECORD
#
# EPISTEMIC STATUS
# ---------------
# Every substantive assertion/material record SHOULD carry an epistemic
# status compatible with the surrounding Humanesque epistemic architecture:
#
# [RETRIEVED]    obtained from a trusted source
# [INFERRED]     logically derived from retrieved material
# [PROPOSED]     hypothesis / design / suggested construction
# [UNRESOLVED]   unknown, inconsistent or insufficiently evidenced
#
# An untagged epistemic statement MUST NOT enter canonical output where
# epistemic tagging is required.
#
# CORE STAGES
# -----------
# The canonical MASI lifecycle is:
#
#   INTAKE
#   IDENTIFY
#   CAPTURE
#   PROVENANCE
#   EPISTEMIC_CLASSIFY
#   EVIDENCE
#   VERIFY
#   GOVERN
#   REVIEW
#   IPR_GATE
#   REGISTER
#   PUBLISH
#   PRESERVE
#
# The lifecycle is not necessarily linear. A stage may cause revision,
# branching, additional evidence collection, or return to an earlier stage.
#
# STAGE 01 — INTAKE
# -----------------
STAGE INTAKE {
    ELICIT research.input
    CAPTURE research.material
    CAPTURE source.context
    CAPTURE submission.mode
    CAPTURE received_at
    CAPTURE actor.identity
    CAPTURE actor.authorization
    CAPTURE originating_cycler
    CAPTURE originating_realm
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 02 — IDENTIFY
# -------------------
STAGE IDENTIFY {
    IDENTIFY research.object
    IDENTIFY artifact.type
    IDENTIFY domain
    IDENTIFY authors
    IDENTIFY contributors
    IDENTIFY source.material
    IDENTIFY parent.records
    IDENTIFY related.cycler.states
    IDENTIFY existing.versions
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 03 — CAPTURE
# ------------------
STAGE CAPTURE {
    CAPTURE content
    CAPTURE metadata
    CAPTURE attachments
    CAPTURE references
    CAPTURE source
    CAPTURE acquisition.time
    CAPTURE event.time WHEN KNOWN
    CAPTURE modality
    CAPTURE representation
    CAPTURE initial.state
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 04 — PROVENANCE
# --------------------
# Critical MASI invariant: human provenance propagates across cyclers.
#
STAGE PROVENANCE {
    CAPTURE human.contributor
    CAPTURE contribution.kind
    CAPTURE contribution.content
    CAPTURE contribution.time
    CAPTURE contribution.source
    CAPTURE contribution.location WHEN AVAILABLE
    CAPTURE contribution.authorization
    CAPTURE contribution.relationship.to_artifact
    CAPTURE originating.cycler
    CAPTURE originating.cycler.state
    CAPTURE upstream.provenance
    CAPTURE downstream.provenance
    CAPTURE transformation.lineage
    CAPTURE branch.lineage
    CAPTURE merge.lineage
    CAPTURE revision.lineage
    CAPTURE version.lineage
    CAPTURE derivative.lineage
    LINK provenance.to.artifact
    LINK provenance.to.human
    LINK provenance.to.cycler
    LINK provenance.to.time
    LINK provenance.to.realm
    LINK provenance.to.evidence
    END STAGE
}
#
# PROVENANCE PROPAGATION RULE
# ---------------------------
RULE HUMAN_PROVENANCE_PERSISTS {
    WHEN artifact.is_derived
    THEN PRESERVE upstream.human.provenance
    AND PRESERVE transformation.lineage
    AND PRESERVE temporal.position
    AND PRESERVE originating.cycler
    AND PRESERVE relevant.intermediate.states
}
#
RULE PROVENANCE_ON_COMPOSITION {
    WHEN artifacts.are_merged
    THEN PRESERVE provenance.of.each.constituent
    AND CREATE composition.record
    AND LINK composition.to.result
}
#
RULE PROVENANCE_ON_BRANCH {
    WHEN artifact.is_branched
    THEN PRESERVE parent.provenance
    AND CREATE branch.relationship
}
#
RULE PROVENANCE_ON_REVISION {
    WHEN artifact.is_revised
    THEN PRESERVE ancestry
    AND CREATE new.version
    AND LINK revision.to.predecessor
}
#
# STAGE 05 — EPISTEMIC CLASSIFICATION
# -----------------------------------
STAGE EPISTEMIC_CLASSIFY {
    CLASSIFY claims AS [RETRIEVED]
    CLASSIFY claims AS [INFERRED]
    CLASSIFY claims AS [PROPOSED]
    CLASSIFY claims AS [UNRESOLVED]
    PRESERVE epistemic.status
    LINK claims.to.sources
    LINK claims.to.evidence
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 06 — EVIDENCE
# -------------------
STAGE EVIDENCE {
    CAPTURE supporting.sources
    CAPTURE evidence.records
    CAPTURE measurements
    CAPTURE references
    CAPTURE checksums WHEN AVAILABLE
    CAPTURE integrity.records
    DISTINGUISH evidence FROM provenance
    DISTINGUISH evidence FROM registration
    DISTINGUISH evidence FROM interpretation
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 07 — VERIFY
# -----------------
STAGE VERIFY {
    VERIFY identity
    VERIFY provenance
    VERIFY integrity
    VERIFY evidence
    VERIFY temporal.records
    VERIFY epistemic.status
    VERIFY authorization
    VERIFY publication.constraints
    VERIFY IPR.constraints
    VERIFY repository.constraints
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 08 — GOVERN
# -----------------
# Research Kundali provides the organizing research trajectory / lineage
# structure used in the Epistemic Realms.
#
STAGE GOVERN {
    UPDATE RESEARCH_KUNDALI
    LINK research.object
    LINK research.trajectory
    LINK research.milestones
    LINK evidence.lineage
    LINK provenance.lineage
    LINK review.history
    LINK revisions
    LINK IPR.events
    LINK registration.events
    LINK publication.events
    CHECK epistemic.cleanliness
    CHECK provenance.completeness
    CHECK unresolved.items
    END STAGE
}
#
# EPISTEMIC REALM CLEANLINESS
# ---------------------------
RULE REALM_CLEANLINESS {
    BEFORE canonical.publication
        VERIFY epistemic.status
        VERIFY source/evidence links
        VERIFY provenance
        VERIFY unresolved.items
        VERIFY review.state
}
#
# STAGE 09 — REVIEW
# -----------------
# Supports peer review, journal review, conference review and equivalent
# research-quality gates.
#
STAGE REVIEW {
    SELECT review.mode
    # review.mode MAY be:
    #   PEER
    #   JOURNAL
    #   CONFERENCE
    #   EDITORIAL
    #   IPR
    #   INTERNAL
    CAPTURE reviewer.identity
    CAPTURE reviewer.role
    CAPTURE review.criteria
    CAPTURE review.comments
    CAPTURE review.decision
    CAPTURE review.time
    LINK review.to.version
    LINK review.to.evidence
    LINK review.to.provenance
    PRESERVE review.history
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 10 — IPR GATE
# -------------------
STAGE IPR_GATE {
    IDENTIFY intellectual.property.claims
    IDENTIFY human.contributions
    IDENTIFY temporal.positions
    IDENTIFY derivative.relationships
    IDENTIFY disclosure.status
    IDENTIFY filing.status
    VERIFY provenance.chain
    VERIFY evidence.chain
    VERIFY authorization
    DETERMINE required.gates
    END STAGE
}
#
# G3 PRE-FILING GATE
# ------------------
STAGE G3 {
    # G3 is a specific pre-filing / disclosure gate within the IPR process.
    CAPTURE invention.or.claim
    CAPTURE contributors
    CAPTURE provenance
    CAPTURE temporal.evidence
    CAPTURE disclosure.state
    CAPTURE supporting.records
    VERIFY prefiling.constraints
    REVIEW IPR.material
    SIGNOFF G3
    END STAGE
}
#
# G3 IS NOT THE WHOLE MASI SYSTEM.
# It is one specific IPR gate within MASI.
#
# TEMPORAL-REALM IPR INVARIANT
# ----------------------------
RULE TEMPORAL_REALM_IPR {
    WHEN humanesque.cycler.operates.inside epistemic.realm
    THEN PRESERVE human.input.identity
    AND PRESERVE human.input.time
    AND PRESERVE input.content.relationship
    AND PRESERVE cycler.identity
    AND PRESERVE cycler.state
    AND PRESERVE transformation.history
    AND PRESERVE derivative.history
    AND PRESERVE evidence.references
    AND MAKE lineage.reconstructible
}
#
# STAGE 11 — REGISTER
# -------------------
STAGE REGISTER {
    ASK registration.path
    IF registration.path == "MISTY_DOI"
        GOTO MISTY_DOI
    ELSE IF registration.path == "TOK_DOI"
        GOTO TOK_DOI
    ELSE
        CAPTURE registration.choice
    END STAGE
}
#
# MISTY DOI — SCHOLARLY / PUBLICATION PATH
# ----------------------------------------
STAGE MISTY_DOI {
    PREPARE publication.metadata
    PREPARE repository.package
    PREPARE provenance.record
    PREPARE integrity.record
    PREPARE version.record
    SELECT repository
    IF repository == "ZENODO"
        SUBMIT repository.package
        CAPTURE zenodo.record
        CAPTURE zenodo.doi
    END
    CREATE misty.doi.record
    LINK misty.doi.record TO artifact
    LINK misty.doi.record TO version
    LINK misty.doi.record TO provenance
    LINK misty.doi.record TO publication
    PRESERVE registration.event
    END STAGE
}
#
# TOK DOI — WEB-NATIVE TEMPORAL REGISTRATION PATH
# ------------------------------------------------
STAGE TOK_DOI {
    # "No sugar added":
    # no token is intrinsically required.
    CAPTURE web.record
    CAPTURE web.content
    CAPTURE web.metadata
    CAPTURE web.source
    CAPTURE registration.time
    REQUEST OTS_TIMESTAMP
    CAPTURE ots.timestamp
    LINK ots.timestamp TO web.record
    LINK web.record TO provenance
    LINK web.record TO artifact
    ASK public.registry
    IF public.registry == TRUE
        SUBMIT registry.record
        CAPTURE registry.state
        CAPTURE registry.position
        CAPTURE registry.occupancy
        CAPTURE registry.frequency
    END
    IF registry.doi.condition == TRUE
        CONVERT registry.state TO DOI
        CAPTURE resulting.doi
    END
    CREATE tok.record
    LINK tok.record TO timestamp
    LINK tok.record TO registry WHEN PRESENT
    LINK tok.record TO artifact
    LINK tok.record TO provenance
    PRESERVE registration.event
    END STAGE
}
#
# TOK REGISTRY POLICY
# -------------------
RULE TOK_REGISTRY_ACCUMULATION {
    # DOI creation is not mandatory for every Tok event.
    # Registry material may accumulate until the configured registry
    # frequency / occupancy condition is met.
    WHEN registry.frequency_or_occupancy.threshold_reached
        THEN CREATE DOI_FROM_REGISTRY_STATE
}
#
# STAGE 12 — PUBLISH
# ------------------
STAGE PUBLISH {
    SELECT publication.target
    # publication.target MAY include:
    #   JOURNAL
    #   CONFERENCE
    #   PREPRINT
    #   REPOSITORY
    #   PATENT/IPR RECORD
    #   PUBLIC REGISTRY
    PREPARE publication.package
    INCLUDE metadata
    INCLUDE provenance
    INCLUDE version
    INCLUDE integrity
    INCLUDE review.history WHEN APPLICABLE
    INCLUDE epistemic.status WHEN REQUIRED
    INCLUDE registration.records
    SUBMIT publication.package
    CAPTURE publication.identity
    CAPTURE publication.time
    END STAGE
}
#
# STAGE 13 — PRESERVE
# -------------------
STAGE PRESERVE {
    SEAL artifact.version
    PRESERVE content
    PRESERVE metadata
    PRESERVE provenance
    PRESERVE evidence
    PRESERVE epistemic.history
    PRESERVE review.history
    PRESERVE IPR.history
    PRESERVE registration.history
    PRESERVE publication.history
    PRESERVE checksums WHEN AVAILABLE
    CREATE audit.record
    END STAGE
}
#
# RESEARCH KUNDALI
# ----------------
OBJECT RESEARCH_KUNDALI {
    identity
    research.object
    domain
    trajectory
    milestones
    events
    claims
    evidence
    sources
    provenance
    contributors
    cycler.states
    versions
    reviews
    revisions
    IPR.events
    G3.events
    registration.events
    publication.events
    preservation.events
    unresolved.items
    epistemic.status
}
#
# RESEARCH KUNDALI OPERATIONS
# ---------------------------
STAGE KUNDALI_UPDATE {
    CAPTURE event
    ORDER event temporally
    LINK event TO research.object
    LINK event TO actor
    LINK event TO cycler
    LINK event TO evidence
    LINK event TO provenance
    LINK event TO prior.events
    LINK event TO subsequent.events
    PRESERVE event
    END STAGE
}
#
# HUMAN CONTRIBUTION RECORD
# -------------------------
OBJECT HUMAN_CONTRIBUTION {
    contributor.identity
    contributor.role
    contribution.type
    contribution.content.reference
    contribution.time
    contribution.context
    originating.cycler
    originating.cycler.state
    originating.realm
    authorization
    transformation.lineage
    derivative.lineage
    publication.lineage
    IPR.lineage
}
#
# CROSS-CYCLER PROVENANCE RECORD
# -----------------------------
OBJECT CROSS_CYCLER_PROVENANCE {
    human.inputs[]
    source.cycler
    source.state
    target.cycler
    target.state
    operation
    transformation
    composition
    branch
    merge
    revision
    version
    temporal.order
    evidence[]
    integrity[]
    authorization[]
}
#
# CYCLER INTEROPERABILITY
# -----------------------
STAGE IMPORT_FROM_CYCLER {
    CAPTURE source.cycler
    CAPTURE source.state
    CAPTURE source.artifact
    CAPTURE source.provenance
    CAPTURE source.temporal.records
    CAPTURE source.epistemic.status
    CAPTURE source.version
    VERIFY imported.records
    LINK imported.artifact TO MASI_RECORD
    PRESERVE source.identity
    END STAGE
}
#
STAGE EXPORT_TO_CYCLER {
    PREPARE approved.material
    INCLUDE provenance
    INCLUDE epistemic.status
    INCLUDE registration.state
    INCLUDE version
    INCLUDE review.state
    LINK export TO source.record
    PRESERVE MASI lineage
    END STAGE
}
#
# PUBLICATION BRANCHES
# --------------------
STAGE JOURNAL {
    CAPTURE manuscript
    CAPTURE journal.target
    REVIEW peer
    REVIEW editorial
    REVISE manuscript
    APPROVE manuscript
    PUBLISH manuscript
    PRESERVE publication.record
    END STAGE
}
#
STAGE CONFERENCE {
    CAPTURE submission
    CAPTURE conference.target
    REVIEW peer
    REVISE submission
    APPROVE submission
    PUBLISH conference.record
    PRESERVE publication.record
    END STAGE
}
#
STAGE PEER_REVIEW {
    CAPTURE review.request
    ASSIGN reviewer
    CAPTURE review
    LINK review TO artifact.version
    CAPTURE decision
    PRESERVE review
    END STAGE
}
#
# IPR / DISCLOSURE BRANCH
# -----------------------
STAGE IPR {
    CAPTURE claim
    CAPTURE contributors
    CAPTURE provenance
    CAPTURE temporal.records
    CAPTURE disclosure.state
    GOTO G3
    IF G3 == APPROVED
        PREPARE filing.package
    ELSE
        REVISE IPR_RECORD
    END
    PRESERVE IPR_RECORD
    END STAGE
}
#
# ITERATION / REVISION
# --------------------
STAGE REVISE {
    CAPTURE revision.reason
    CAPTURE changed.material
    PRESERVE predecessor
    CREATE new.version
    PROPAGATE provenance
    PROPAGATE epistemic.status
    INVALIDATE dependent.records WHEN REQUIRED
    RETURN REVIEW
    END STAGE
}
#
# AUDIT
# -----
STAGE AUDIT {
    CHECK identity
    CHECK provenance
    CHECK evidence
    CHECK temporal.order
    CHECK version.history
    CHECK review.history
    CHECK IPR.history
    CHECK registration.history
    CHECK publication.history
    CHECK preservation.state
    CREATE audit.record
    END STAGE
}
#
# FAILURE / SAFETY RULES
# ----------------------
RULE NEVER_DROP_HUMAN_PROVENANCE {
    IF transformation.removes_human.attribution
        THEN HALT
        AND RETURN PROVENANCE
}
#
RULE NEVER_CONFUSE_REGISTRATION_WITH_PROVENANCE {
    registration.record != provenance.record
}
#
RULE NEVER_CONFUSE_EVIDENCE_WITH_PROVENANCE {
    evidence.record != provenance.record
}
#
RULE NEVER_CONFUSE_TIMESTAMP_WITH_IPR_OWNERSHIP {
    timestamp.record != ownership.determination
}
#
RULE NEVER_TREAT_TOK_AS_MANDATORY_DOI {
    Tok.registration MAY EXIST without immediate DOI
}
#
RULE NEVER_TREAT_G3_AS_WHOLE_MASI {
    G3 IS_SUBPROCESS_OF MASI
}
#
RULE PRESERVE_ANCESTRY {
    revision OR branch OR merge OR transformation
        MUST preserve relevant predecessor links
}
#
RULE NO_UNTAGGED_CANONICAL_CLAIM {
    IF claim.epistemic_status == NULL
        THEN HOLD_FOR_CLASSIFICATION
}
#
# CANONICAL END-TO-END FLOWS
# --------------------------
#
# A. RESEARCH / SCHOLARLY PUBLICATION
#
FLOW SCHOLARLY {
    INTAKE
    IDENTIFY
    CAPTURE
    PROVENANCE
    EPISTEMIC_CLASSIFY
    EVIDENCE
    VERIFY
    GOVERN
    REVIEW
    IPR_GATE WHEN APPLICABLE
    REGISTER
    PUBLISH
    PRESERVE
}
#
# B. TOK TEMPORAL REGISTRATION
#
FLOW TOK {
    INTAKE
    IDENTIFY
    CAPTURE
    PROVENANCE
    EPISTEMIC_CLASSIFY
    VERIFY
    GOVERN
    TOK_DOI
    PRESERVE
}
#
# C. MISTY DOI
#
FLOW MISTY {
    INTAKE
    IDENTIFY
    CAPTURE
    PROVENANCE
    EPISTEMIC_CLASSIFY
    EVIDENCE
    VERIFY
    GOVERN
    REVIEW WHEN APPLICABLE
    MISTY_DOI
    PUBLISH
    PRESERVE
}
#
# D. IPR / G3
#
FLOW IPR_G3 {
    INTAKE
    IDENTIFY
    CAPTURE
    PROVENANCE
    EVIDENCE
    VERIFY
    GOVERN
    IPR_GATE
    G3
    AUDIT
    PRESERVE
}
#
# E. CROSS-CYCLER HUMAN CONTRIBUTION
#
FLOW CROSS_CYCLER {
    IMPORT_FROM_CYCLER
    PROVENANCE
    EPISTEMIC_CLASSIFY
    EVIDENCE
    VERIFY
    GOVERN
    REVIEW WHEN APPLICABLE
    REGISTER WHEN APPLICABLE
    EXPORT_TO_CYCLER WHEN APPLICABLE
    PRESERVE
}
#
# F. PUBLICATION REVIEW LOOP
#
FLOW REVIEW_LOOP {
    REVIEW
    IF decision == "REVISE"
        GOTO REVISE
    IF decision == "APPROVE"
        GOTO REGISTER
    IF decision == "REJECT"
        PRESERVE review.record
        END
}
#
# OUTPUTS
# -------
# MASI can produce / govern:
#
#   research records
#   provenance records
#   epistemic records
#   review records
#   journal packages
#   conference packages
#   repository packages
#   IPR records
#   G3 records
#   Misty DOI records
#   Tok temporal-registration records
#   public registry records
#   publication identities
#   audit records
#   preservation packages
#
# CONFORMANCE
# -----------
# A Misty MASI implementation conforms only if it can:
#
#   1. distinguish human input from cycler transformation;
#   2. preserve human provenance across cycler boundaries;
#   3. maintain temporal ordering / event history;
#   4. maintain artifact/version ancestry;
#   5. distinguish evidence, provenance, registration and interpretation;
#   6. support epistemic governance through Research Kundali;
#   7. support research review workflows;
#   8. support IPR workflows and G3 pre-filing gating;
#   9. support both Misty DOI and Tok DOI paths;
#  10. preserve records after publication/registration;
#  11. remain interoperable with independent Humanesque cyclers;
#  12. preserve provenance through composition, branching, merging and revision.
#
# CANONICAL SUMMARY
# -----------------
# MISTY MASI =
#   identity
# + provenance
# + epistemic governance
# + research trajectory
# + evidence
# + review
# + IPR gating
# + temporal registration
# + publication
# + preservation
#
# MISTY DOI:
#   scholarly/publication route -> repository/Zenodo -> DOI
#
# TOK DOI:
#   web record -> OTS timestamp -> optional public registry
#   -> DOI when registry policy triggers conversion
#
# CORE INVARIANT:
#   HUMAN INPUT
#       -> CYCLER
#       -> TRANSFORMATION(S)
#       -> COMPOSITION / REVISION / DERIVATION
#       -> REGISTER / PUBLISH
#       -> PRESERVE
#
#   HUMAN PROVENANCE MUST REMAIN TRACEABLE THROUGH THE ENTIRE CHAIN.
#
# END MISTY MASI PNI
